› uai voce nao vai fazer nao ? o plano ' # Aquamarine MS912X CPU-Blit Fallback Plan

    ## Summary

    - Keep Omarchy/Hyprland as the target desktop.
    - Treat the MS912X kernel driver as fixed: it now exposes only 1920x1080@29.98Hz, and Hyprland can modeset it.
    - Patch Aquamarine 0.11.0 because the failure is in its multi-GPU blit path: it tries to create an EGL renderer for /dev/dri/card0 even though ms912x has no render node.
    - Add a CPU fallback path for secondary DRM devices without an EGL-capable render node.

    References:

    - Aquamarine env docs: https://wiki.hypr.land/Hypr-Ecosystem/aquamarine/
    - Aquamarine source: https://github.com/hyprwm/aquamarine/blob/v0.11.0/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp
    - Renderer source: https://github.com/hyprwm/aquamarine/blob/v0.11.0/src/backend/drm/Renderer.cpp

    ## Key Changes

    - Add one low-risk config test before patching:
        - Set AQ_FORCE_LINEAR_BLIT=1 or verify default behavior with AQ_TRACE=1.
        - Retest activate-usb-monitor.sh.
        - Continue to patch if logs still show CDRMRenderer(drm): Can't create renderer, no matching devices found.
    - Build a local patched aquamarine 0.11.0-2 package:
        - Use the Arch package source or upstream v0.11.0.
        - Keep ABI/package version compatible with installed hyprland 0.54.3-4.
        - Install as a pacman package, not by manually copying .so files.
    - Patch Aquamarine’s DRM backend:
        - In CDRMBackend::initMgpu(), detect secondary GPUs with no render node where CDRMRenderer::attempt() fails.
        - For those devices, allow a “CPU blit” fallback instead of failing the output.
        - Use CDRMDumbAllocator for the MS912X scanout buffer.
        - Use the primary i915 renderer to readBuffer() the rendered frame into CPU memory.
        - Copy that CPU RGBA/XRGB data into the dumb buffer via beginDataPtr() / endDataPtr().
        - Submit the dumb buffer to KMS with the existing CDRMFB::create() path.
    - Keep existing Hyprland config:
        - AQ_DRM_DEVICES=/dev/dri/card2:/dev/dri/card0
        - AQ_NO_MODIFIERS=1
        - AQ_MGPU_NO_EXPLICIT=1
        - AQ_NO_ATOMIC=1
        - monitor = HDMI-A-3, disable at login
        - Manual activation through ~/.config/hypr/scripts/activate-usb-monitor.sh

    ## Test Plan

    - Build validation:
        - Build patched Aquamarine cleanly with makepkg.
        - Confirm pacman -Q aquamarine still reports compatible 0.11.0.
        - Confirm Hyprland starts normally with notebook + HDMI NVIDIA only.
    - MS912X activation test:
        - Run ~/.config/hypr/scripts/activate-usb-monitor.sh.
        - Expected Hyprland state:
            - HDMI-A-3 enabled
            - 1920x1080@29.98Hz
            - currentFormat: XRGB8888
        - Expected log state:
            - No repeated Can't create renderer, no matching devices found
            - New CPU fallback log line appears for card0/ms912x
            - No rollback by the activation script
    - Visual test:
        - Monitor no longer stays black after activation.
        - Moving a window to workspace/output 3 shows real desktop content.
        - If performance is poor, keep it acceptable for static/low-motion use; USB 2.0 latency is expected.
    - Rollback:
        - Reinstall the official Arch aquamarine package from cache or pacman if the patched build breaks Hyprland.
        - Keep HDMI-A-3 disabled at login so a failed patch cannot trap the desktop in a black-screen loop.

    ## Assumptions

    - The first goal is a working Hyprland extended desktop on the USB HDMI monitor, even if it is slower.
    - We will not change the MS912X kernel driver unless the patched Aquamarine path proves it needs a different framebuffer format.
    - The first CPU fallback target is XRGB8888/linear dumb buffers only; no broad multi-format support unless tests prove it is necessary.
    - NVIDIA remains excluded from AQ_DRM_DEVICES because Aquamarine reports /dev/dri/card1 is not a KMS device on this laptop.
